% British citizenship over time: sections 1(1) and 12 of the
% British Nationality Act 1981, in Logical English for LPS.
%
%     12.-(1) If any British citizen of full age and capacity makes in the
%     prescribed manner a declaration of renunciation of British citizenship,
%     then, subject to subsections (3) and (4), the Secretary of State shall
%     cause the declaration to be registered.
%     (2) On the registration of a declaration made in pursuance of this
%     section the person who made it shall cease to be a British citizen.
%     (3) A declaration made by a person in pursuance of this section shall
%     not be registered unless the Secretary of State is satisfied that the
%     person who made it will after the registration have or acquire some
%     citizenship or nationality other than British citizenship; ...

the target language is: lps.

the maximum time is 9.

the events are:
    *a person* is born in the UK to *a parent*.
    *a person* declares renunciation.
    *a person* acquires another nationality.

the actions are:
    the Secretary of State registers the declaration of *a person*.

the fluents are:
    *a person* is a British citizen.
    *a person* is settled in the UK.
    *a person* has another nationality.

the knowledge base British Nationality Act includes:

initially mary is a British citizen.

when a person is born in the UK to a parent
    and the parent is a British citizen
then the person is a British citizen.

when a person is born in the UK to a parent
    and the parent is settled in the UK
then the person is a British citizen.

when a person acquires another nationality
then the person has another nationality.

if a person is a British citizen at a first time
    and the person declares renunciation from the first time to a second time
then the Secretary of State registers the declaration of the person from a third time to a fourth time.

when the Secretary of State registers the declaration of a person
then it is not the case that the person is a British citizen.

it must not be true that
    the Secretary of State registers the declaration of a person
    and it is not the case that the person has another nationality.

scenario john is:
    john is born in the UK to mary from 1 to 2.
    john declares renunciation from 3 to 4.
    john acquires another nationality from 6 to 7.
